        details = "Keeps: mutual ownership from Cooperative economy (Japan's mutual life insurers; Friendly societies as approved societies in Britain); union-run funds with public money from Nordic social democracy (Union-run unemployment funds (the Ghent system)); payouts to injured workers from Corporatism and fascist economics (Bismarck's compulsory accident insurance); mutual risk equalisation from Social market economy (Compulsory sickness funds in the Netherlands); the mutual guarantee from Islamic economics (Takaful, the first Islamic mutual insurers). Blocks: cover tied to employment, safeguarded by income-based contributions for every resident; group rating that dulls prevention, safeguarded by part of each premium set by the firm's record; uncovered catastrophic risk, safeguarded by a public backstop. Test: over several years, count residents without cover for illness, injury or job loss, compare firms' accident rates before and after rating, and check reserves each year. Source: Senshu University paper; Royal Commission report; Cambridge-hosted article; Guinnane and Streb (2015); Vonk (2012); Pew article (2016); Atlas takaful article.",
